/-!
# Very tame quotients of log regular pairs

Source: ILO, Exposé VI, Theorem 3.2 and Proposition 3.5(c), pp. 73--75;
VI 1.4 and the quotient-pair application in IX 2.4, p. 134
(blueprint: lem-per-very-tame-quotient-log-regular).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A very tame quotient carries the invariant divisorial log structure, which is
fs log regular, has precisely the complement of the image boundary as its triviality
locus, and makes that boundary a log regular pair. The section isomorphisms specify
`(q_* M_D)^G` on every étale test object, compatibly with its structural map;
compatibility forces naturality because pullback into the invariant ring is injective.

Source: ILO VI 3.2, 3.5(c), 3.7(a)--(c), VI 1.4 and IX 2.4
(blueprint: lem-per-very-tame-quotient-log-regular).

Proof:
1. Put N = (q_* M_D)^G. Its structural map lands in the invariant ring O_Y.
   Invariant sections mapping to units are exactly invariant units, so N is a log
   structure. By lem-per-finite-quotient-strict-local-invariants, Y is Noetherian,
   geometric fibres are orbits and, at a lift of each geometric point, B = A^H,
   A is finite over B and N's stalk is the invariant divisorial stalk M^H.
2. Set Q = M/Aˣ and I equal to the nonunit ideal. Log regularity gives regular A/I
   and dim A = dim(A/I) + rank Q^gp. Very tameness makes |H| invertible and the
   actions on Q and A/I trivial. Apply lem-per-very-tame-equivariant-sharp-chart
   to obtain the sharp equivariant chart with diagonal character χ. In this chart
   the nonunit ideal is generated by a(q) for q ≠ 0.
3. Apply lem-per-very-tame-local-kummer-quotient. The invariant chart is the sharp
   fs monoid P = Q ∩ L, where L is the common character kernel, P^gp = L and
   |H| Q^gp ⊆ L. With J generated by a(p), p ≠ 0, it gives B/J ≅ A/I.
   The neighbourhood clause gives actual étale-local charts of N, proving fs.
4. Finiteness and injectivity imply dim B = dim A by
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral and
   lem-weil-pbc-integral-injective-dimension-equal. The finite-index inclusion gives
   rank P^gp = rank Q^gp after tensoring with ℚ. Substitute into Step 2 to obtain
   dim B = dim(B/J) + rank P^gp; the isomorphism gives regular B/J. This is log regularity.
5. P is trivial exactly when Q is: if P is trivial, |H|q = 0 for every q, and a
   saturated sharp monoid has torsion-free group completion (saturation makes a
   torsion element and its negative units, then sharpness kills them). Thus the
   triviality locus is Y minus q(E); E is invariant and fibres are orbits.
   By lem-trf-log-regular-divisorial-structure this locus is open dense and N is
   its divisorial log structure. This proves the asserted log regular pair,
   using def-trf-log-regular-pair, with exactly the same boundary q(E). -/
theorem veryTame_quotient_logRegular
    (D Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral D] [IsNoetherian D]
    (U : D.Opens) (hU : DenseRange U.ι)
    (hlog : IsDivisorialFineSaturatedLogRegularPair D U.toScheme U.ι hU)
    (G : Type v) [Group G] [Finite G] (a : G →* Aut D)
    (hpres : ∀ (g : G) (x : D), (a g).hom x ∈ U ↔ x ∈ U)
    (hfree : ∃ V : D.Opens, Dense (V : Set D) ∧
      (∀ (g : G) (x : D), (a g).hom x ∈ V ↔ x ∈ V) ∧
      ∀ (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] (t : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ D),
        (Scheme.SpecToEquivOfField Ω D t).1 ∈ V →
          ∀ g : G, t ≫ (a g).hom = t → g = 1)
    (htame : IsVeryTameDivisorialAction U a)
    (q : D ⟶ Y) (hquot : IsAdmissibleFiniteSchemeQuotient a q) :
    ∃ (hY : IsLocallyNoetherian Y) (N : EtaleLogStructure Y)
      (hfs : N.IsFineSaturated),
      (∀ W : Y.Etale,
        ∃ e : N.monoidSheaf.obj.obj (op W) ≃*
            invariantDivisorialDirectImageSections U a q hquot.2.2.1 W,
          ∀ s : N.monoidSheaf.obj.obj (op W),
            (pullback.fst W.hom q).appTop (N.alpha.app (op W) s) = (e s).val) ∧
      (FineSaturatedLogScheme.mk Y hY N hfs).IsLogRegular ∧
      N.trivialityLocus = (q '' ((U : Set D)ᶜ))ᶜ ∧
      ∃ (V : Y.Opens) (hV : DenseRange V.ι),
        (V : Set Y) = (q '' ((U : Set D)ᶜ))ᶜ ∧
          @IsDivisorialFineSaturatedLogRegularPair Y V.toScheme V.ι inferInstance hY hV := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
